WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.452
A RAG request is easier to understand when we follow one concrete question.

00:00:05.452 --> 00:00:14.082
Suppose the user asks, “What is the refund deadline?” The retriever finds a chunk stating that refund requests must be

00:00:14.082 --> 00:00:16.612
submitted within fourteen days.

00:00:16.612 --> 00:00:24.032
The application formats that chunk, builds a prompt telling the L L M to use only the supplied context,

00:00:24.032 --> 00:00:27.037
and sends the final tokenized request.

00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:31.922
From the model's point of view, the vector database is no longer visible.

00:00:31.922 --> 00:00:35.013
It only sees the prompt your application assembled.
